---
Read and write one `kv` store through the target's own backend, with no flow (validates, builds, then launches)

Usage: agent-compose store <COMMAND>

Commands:
  get     Read one key: the value it holds and its version (exit 1 when it holds nothing)
  set     Write one key, held to the store's `value_schema` first (exit 1 when a condition declines)
  delete  Delete one key (exit 1 when `--if-version` declines)
  list    List one page of keys, in byte order
  count   Count the keys the partition holds
  export  Write every live entry as JSON Lines on stdout: `{ key, value, version, expires_at }`
  import  Write the entries of an export, read from standard input or `--file`, at fresh versions
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help
